GATE G0 — NESTOR CASH-FEED READER
=================================================================================================
STATUS: **NOT APPLIED.** This is a proposal diff against `crates/engine/src/reconcile.rs`.
It takes its OWN review gate (spec §7 G0, SF-4) and is deliberately shipped as a file rather
than as a commit on the v5 branch, so that reviewing v5 and reviewing this are two separate
acts by two separate reviewers.

WHAT IT DOES
  Adds `data/lip_cash_feed.json` to the breaker's `(ext_cash, ext_pending)` pair, behind the
  environment flag `LIP_CASH_FEED_ENABLED`, **default FALSE (IGNORE)**.

WHY A SECOND FILE AT ALL (spec §5.1)
  nestor's breaker SUMS every line of `data/external_cash.jsonl` (`read_external_cash`, this
  file). A cumulative computed value appended THERE would double-count against the operator's
  hand rows, and two writers on one file is a collision. So v5 owns a separate single-object
  file, rewritten atomically, and `external_cash.jsonl` survives untouched for non-LIP flows
  (deposits, the FOMC strangle).

WHY IT IS INERT UNTIL THE FLAG FLIPS
  With the flag false this is dead code: `read_lip_cash_feed()` returns `(0.0, 0.0)` before it
  touches the filesystem, so `divergence` is byte-identical to today. That is the G0 read-out.

THE THREE SAFETY PROPERTIES, EACH LOAD-BEARING
  1. **Staleness pages, never halts** (spec §5.4). If `now − ts > 120 s` we KEEP the last value
     and alert. Halting on a stale feed would convert *v5 dying* into *nestor dying* — the
     precise failure this whole interface exists to prevent.
  2. **A malformed or foreign-schema file contributes (0, 0)**, loudly. It never contributes a
     partial parse: a half-understood cash number is worse than none.
  3. **An ABSENT file is (0, 0)**, which is correct only if v5 is truly flat — and v5's SIGTERM
     path guarantees that by writing a final ZEROED feed after cancel-all + shed, and only then
     may the file be removed (spec §5.4's mirror).

REVIEW CHECKLIST FOR THE G0 REVIEWER
  [ ] With `LIP_CASH_FEED_ENABLED` unset, `divergence` is byte-identical across ≥1 reconcile
      pass (the flag's whole purpose).
  [ ] With it true and a hand-built feed file, `expected_cash` moves by exactly the feed's
      `delta_dollars`, and `pending_payout` by exactly `pending_payout_dollars`.
  [ ] The staleness branch does NOT halt.
  [ ] `external_cash.jsonl` behaviour is unchanged in every branch.
  [ ] Rollback is `unset LIP_CASH_FEED_ENABLED` — a one-line revert, no redeploy.

ROLLBACK: flag false. The reader is inert code until then.
